NAME
       seq - print a sequence of numbers

SYNOPSIS
       seq [-w] [-s SEP] [-f FORMAT] [FIRST [INCREMENT]] LAST

DESCRIPTION
       Print numbers from FIRST to LAST in steps of INCREMENT (both default to
       1).

OPTIONS
       -w
           equalize width by padding with leading zeroes

       -s SEP
           use SEP to separate numbers

       -f FORMAT
           use printf style floating-point FORMAT

EXAMPLES
       seq 5
       seq 0 0.5 2
       seq -w 1 10

SEE ALSO
       yes(1)
